<title>USA: LaBarge wins $2.9-million supply contract.</title>
<headline>LaBarge wins $2.9-million supply contract.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaBarge Inc said Wednesday it won a one-year contract worth $2.9 million from Sensis Corp of DeWitt, New York.</p>
<p>LaBarge will produce printed circuit board assemblies for use in a recently redesigned radar system for the U.S. Marine Corps being built by Sensis, the company said.</p>
<p>LaBarge designs and manufactures custom electronic products and interconnect systems for the telecommunications, medical, aerospace and defense markets.</p>
<p>Its shares closed down 1/4 Wednesday at 5-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
